scripturesstudio (0.49) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Video.py shadowing Asset.py's absolute ASSETS_FOLDER/OUTPUT_FOLDER/
    BUILD_FOLDER with its own relative-string versions, which broke video
    export whenever the app's cwd wasn't the repo root (missing background
    asset and word-highlight slide images).
  * Fix AudioBible.py's installed ORIGINAL_AUDIO_FOLDER/CLONED_AUDIO_FOLDER/
    ENGLISH_AUDIO_FOLDER paths and original_mp3()/cloned_mp3()/english_mp3()
    to match the current audiobible package layout
    (/usr/share/audiobible/<shmueloff|shmueloff-darkknox2|english>/<book>/
    <chapter>/<verse>.mp3), replacing the stale /var/lib/audiobible/
    {original,cloned} flat-filename layout from before that package was
    restructured; CSV files (original.csv, cloned.csv, alignment.csv,
    english.csv) remain under /var/lib/audiobible/ where they're packaged.
  * Fix psalm() route opening 'descriptions.md' via a bare relative path
    (never shipped, never found at runtime); now opens it via Asset.ROOT
    and it's added to scripturesstudio.install.

 -- Reuben Institute <reubeninstitute@gmail.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:05:00 +0300

scripturesstudio (0.48) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Switch packaging from packaging/deb/ (dpkg-deb --build) to a proper
    debian/ source package (dpkg-buildpackage) with debhelper.
  * Drop legacy audiobible-shmueloff-original, audiobible-shmueloff-darkknox2,
    audiobible-darkknox2-english and audiobible-titles submodules and
    dependencies; depend on audiobible instead, and recommend
    audiobible-shmueloff-source for continued audio production work.

